Installation

1. Clone the repository

git clone https://github.com/zakhar-kontsevyi/To-Do-app.git
cd To-Do-app


2. Environment Variables
Change secret key in .env file in the project root:

secret_key=change_me
           ^^^^^^^^^


3. Create a virtual environment

python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate


4. Install dependencies

pip install -r requirements.txt


---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


Running the Application
Start the development server with:

uvicorn main:app --reload

The API will be available at:

http://127.0.0.1:8000


Docker
You need (Docker version 29.6.2 or more) and (Docker Compose version v5.5.1 or more)
The repository includes a Dockerfile and compose.yaml.
To start the application using Docker Compose:

docker compose up --build

To run it in the background:

docker compose up -d --build

Stop the containers with:

docker compose down


---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


API Overview

Authentication
The authentication router is responsible for user registration and login.

Typical flow:

POST /auth/register
POST /auth/login


Tasks
The task router provides operations for managing user tasks.

Typical operations include:

GET    /tasks
POST   /tasks
GET    /tasks/{task_id}
PUT    /tasks/{task_id}
DELETE /tasks/{task_id}

Check the Swagger documentation at http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs for the exact endpoint paths, request schemas, and response formats supported by the current version.


---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


Testing
The project contains a dedicated tests/ directory.

Run the test suite with:

python -m pytest -v





